"## Summary\n\nSecurity-ops follow-up 18: SECOPS-F17-01, under D-160, with the D-098 archive of run `b2de46c8` and one live AT29 run.\n- **Session:** launched 02:29 EST on 2026-11-04 on #460's roadmap row, and delivered at 03:23.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 6 commits and 217 owned files, +444,358/−5,425.\n  - The harness change is 18 files in `tests/e2e/at/secops/` and `mk/at-secops.mk`, +855/−24.\n  - The rest is records: the D-098 archive, the pre-subject incident's archive and the new run's immutable evidence.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (after #463) with this branch and members 22 merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/at-secops.mk at-secops-lint at-secops-test at-secops-build`: the Go tests, 45 Python tests, and the amd64 and arm64 builds;\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`;\n    - `go vet ./...` and `go vet -tags e2e ./tests/e2e/...`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - the committed-evidence tests (`TestCommitted*` in `tests/netlab`, `tests/e2e` and `tests/e2e/at/...`);\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** one live run in the lane's own namespace, after one allowed pre-subject rerun, and no reservation. No product code, database edit or other lane's file changed. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The diagnosis came first.** Run `b2de46c8`'s old killed-agent `lease_expiry` case used a stale cached deadline.\n  - Its two held admission checks were retries of one read, not two separately held commands.\n  - Its records show no overrun of an accepted deadline.\n  - The renewed lease's ID and signed issue time were not retained, and the lane does not invent them.\n- **The change: D is read at the fault.**\n  - After the control stop, the case reads D from the node's accepted local lease and its serving heartbeat.\n  - It requires a 60 s signed cap, a lifetime in (0, 60 s] and a matching future monotonic D. The earlier grant end wins.\n  - **Unchanged:** every traffic predicate, the three-second diagnostic, the D + 3 s bound, the ten-second quiet requirement, recovery and attribution.\n- **D-160 is committed harness code.**\n  - **The protocol:**\n    - an admission journal;\n    - a free admission check immediately before each of six named timed sections;\n    - inside a section, execution receipts only, never an admission check;\n    - an offline validator that fails any run with an admission check inside a section.\n  - **This run:** 509 checks, 507 free and 2 held. Both held checks came after the old case's section ended, at 07:53:41Z and 07:54:41Z, so none overlapped a section.\n    - They were held by the orchestrator's own verification reservation, which it released at 07:54:55Z.\n    - They cost 120 s of waiting between sub-cases.\n- **A pre-subject incident, contained and retained.**\n  - The first dispatch stopped before setup. The new admission helper inherited the wrapped `PATH` and invoked itself recursively.\n  - The lane stopped its 11,215 owned descendant processes and signalled no foreign process. The inventory was zero afterwards.\n  - The fix runs admission with the unwrapped `PATH`, with a regression test and a nested admission smoke check.\n  - The one allowed pre-subject rerun produced the completed run. No sub-case was retried.\n- **Run `9d927350`, 07:47–08:02Z: SECOPS-F17-01 is answered.**\n  - **The old case,** on lease `103d521b` (generation 13, signed cap and lifetime 60 s):\n    - the control stop ended at 07:52:29.33Z, and D was read 90 ms later, with 58.48 s remaining;\n    - the agent was killed at 07:52:32.69Z;\n    - the watchdog's `heartbeat_stale` at 07:53:00.93Z withdrew the rules first. Both transports' last replies were at D − 26.2 s;\n    - the first quiet sample after D was at D + 0.39 s, and the final quiet samples held;\n    - recovery and the